---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../../components/PageHead.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---

<Base title="Privacy policy">
  <PageHead title="Privacy policy" lead="English translation for convenience. The German version (Datenschutzerklärung) is legally binding." />
  <article class="narrow prose">
    <h2>I. Contact details</h2>
    <p>
      The controller responsible for data protection is the medical practice of Dr. Jelena Tomic and Dr. med. Ilsemarie Horst,<br />
      {site.street}, {site.zip} {site.city}, Germany<br />
      Phone: {site.phoneIntl}<br />
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
    </p>

    <h2>II. Processing of personal data</h2>
    <p>
      The controller processes personal data in connection with operating this website. We only process as much data as necessary and always treat
      your data confidentially.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you visit the website, the browser on your device automatically sends information to the server of the website's hosting provider. This
      information is stored temporarily in a so-called log file. The following information is stored automatically:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>the IP address of the requesting computer – anonymised by deleting the last digits,</li>
      <li>the date and time of access,</li>
      <li>the name and URL of the file requested,</li>
      <li>the website from which the access was made (referrer URL),</li>
      <li>the browser used and, where applicable, your computer's operating system and the name of your access provider.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>III. Purposes and legal basis of processing</h2>
    <p>The data is processed only for the following purposes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>ensuring a smooth connection to the website,</li>
      <li>ensuring convenient use of the website,</li>
      <li>evaluating system security and stability, and</li>
      <li>other administrative purposes.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The legal basis for this processing is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest). Our legitimate interest follows from the purposes listed
      above. Under no circumstances do we use the collected data to draw conclusions about you personally.
    </p>
    <p>
      Data you voluntarily send us when contacting us by email (e.g. your name and email address) is processed only as far as necessary for further
      correspondence with you or to meet statutory retention obligations. The legal basis for this processing is Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR.
    </p>
    <p>Personal data collected is deleted or blocked as soon as the purpose of processing no longer applies.</p>

    <h2>IV. Disclosure to third parties</h2>
    <p>Your personal data is not passed on to third parties for any purposes other than those listed below.</p>
    <p>We only pass your personal data on to third parties if:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>you have given your express consent under Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR,</li>
      <li>
        disclosure under Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR is necessary to establish, exercise or defend legal claims and there is no reason to assume that you have
        an overriding legitimate interest in your data not being disclosed,
      </li>
      <li>there is a legal obligation to disclose under Art. 6(1)(c) GDPR, or</li>
      <li>this is legally permitted and necessary under Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR to perform a contract with you.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>V. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You have the right to access the personal data processed about you and to have it rectified, erased or its processing restricted. You also
      have the right to object to processing based on legitimate interest, and the right to data portability. If processing is based on your
      express consent, you can withdraw that consent at any time; an informal email to us is sufficient. Withdrawal does not affect the lawfulness of
      processing carried out before it.
    </p>
    <p>
      You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority. The authority responsible for us is the data protection
      commissioner of Lower Saxony (Die Landesbeauftragte für den Datenschutz Niedersachsen), available at
      <a href="https://www.lfd.niedersachsen.de" rel="noopener">www.lfd.niedersachsen.de</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Data controllers</h2>
    <p>
      Dr. Jelena Tomic<br />
      Dr. Ilsemarie Horst
    </p>

    <h2>Opt-in / opt-out</h2>
    <p>
      General information on withdrawal and objection ("opt-out"): users can withdraw any consent they have given at any time and object to
      processing in accordance with the law. Among other things, users can restrict the use of cookies in their browser settings (although this may
      limit the functionality of our website).
    </p>
    <p>Legal bases: legitimate interests (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR), consent (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR).</p>

    <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      Despite careful checks, we accept no liability for the content of external links. The operators of linked pages are solely responsible for
      their content. You can recognise an external link because your browser's address bar no longer shows www.hausarzt-immensen.de.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
